Chapter: TextOverflowRender
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites UI chapter PixelBuf
  cites UI chapter TextOverflow
  cites Guios chapter GuiDisplay

 The behaviour is arithmetic and is pinned on its own in lib/text-overflow.
 What this asserts is that the renderer OBEYS it: that the walk stops at the
 bound, and that the three modes put different glyphs on the screen rather
 than merely computing different numbers.

 The subject string is sixteen 'w' followed by eight 'i'. A 'w' lights many
 pixels and an 'i' lights few, so clip (which keeps the head) and scroll
 (which keeps the tail) are told apart by ink alone, without reading glyphs.

Section: Body

  buf-w : Integer = 200
  buf-h : Integer = 20
  bound : Integer = 80

  subject : Text = "wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwiiiiiiii"

  ink-row : GopBuf, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ink-row (gb) (y) (x) (xend) (bg) (acc) =
    if x >= xend then acc
    else ink-row gb y (x + 1) xend bg (acc + (if gop-buf-get gb x y == bg then 0 else 1))

  ink : GopBuf, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ink (gb) (y) (x0) (x1) (bg) (acc) =
    if y >= buf-h then acc
    else ink gb (y + 1) x0 x1 bg (acc + ink-row gb y x0 x1 bg 0)

  render : TextOverflow -> Integer
  render (mode) =
    let gb = gop-buf-new buf-w buf-h 0
    in let d = gop-buf-put-text-fit gb 0 2 bound subject 16777215 mode
    in ink gb 0 0 bound 0 0

  spill : TextOverflow -> Integer
  spill (mode) =
    let gb = gop-buf-new buf-w buf-h 0
    in let d = gop-buf-put-text-fit gb 0 2 bound subject 16777215 mode
    in ink gb 0 bound buf-w 0 0

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "nothing may be drawn past the bound, whatever the mode:"
    print-line-uni ("  clip     spill=" & show (spill OverflowClip))
    print-line-uni ("  ellipsis spill=" & show (spill OverflowEllipsis))
    print-line-uni ("  scroll   spill=" & show (spill OverflowScroll))
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "and the three modes must draw DIFFERENT glyphs, not just differ on paper:"
    print-line-uni ("  clip     ink=" & show (render OverflowClip))
    print-line-uni ("  ellipsis ink=" & show (render OverflowEllipsis))
    print-line-uni ("  scroll   ink=" & show (render OverflowScroll))
  end

